    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0389" n="[389]" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg389"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brown to Mr.
                            Seward</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract.]</note>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of
                            the United States</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 11, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I do not believe that any agents of the “Confederate States” have, as yet,
                    visited this place, and should any come here that the Porte would admit or <pb
                        facs="0390" n="390" xml:id="pg390"/> recognize them. I receive from H. H.
                    Aali Pacha, minister of foreign affairs, and H. H. Mehemed Kibrish Pacha, grand
                    vizier, repeated assurances of the most friendly sentiments towards the
                    government of the United States, and expressions of warm sympathy for the
                    present unhappy state of popular excitement in the slave States of the
                    Union.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN P. BROWN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
